WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.100
The content of your own site, such as help articles, products or news,

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.258
can be knowledge for an assistant.

00:00:07.258 --> 00:00:11.466
This video shows how a data source turns a content index into knowledge,

00:00:11.466 --> 00:00:15.619
keeps it in step when the content changes, and lets an assistant answer

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:17.130
from it, with sources.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.913
Large or changing content does not fit as uploaded files.

00:00:25.913 --> 00:00:30.560
Nobody wants to upload every article again each time it changes.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.334
Your site already keeps that content in a search index, so the content

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.710
is ready to be read.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.381
A data source reads that index, splits the content into passages, and keeps

00:00:42.381 --> 00:00:45.480
the knowledge in step as the content changes.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:51.890
The assistant then answers from the passages, and lists numbered sources under its answer.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:59.640
The source index is the content index of your site.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.750
It already exists, or you create it from your content types.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.530
The knowledge base index is the destination.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.650
It stores the passages that the assistant searches by meaning.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:17.044
The data source links the two, and maps which fields hold the content,

00:01:17.044 --> 00:01:19.550
the title and the key of each item.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.930
A profile then chooses the data source, and the assistant answers from it.

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.471
First, the content index.

00:01:31.471 --> 00:01:38.033
Open Search, Indexes, click Add index, and click Add on Content in Elasticsearch.

00:01:38.486 --> 00:01:43.525
Enter an Index Name and a Name, and tick the content types to index.

00:01:43.525 --> 00:01:45.228
Here it is Article.

00:01:45.228 --> 00:01:46.386
Click Save.

00:01:49.813 --> 00:01:52.714
The index fills from the content items.

00:01:52.714 --> 00:01:57.873
To fill it again at any time, open its Actions menu and click Synchronize.

00:02:02.063 --> 00:02:03.929
Next, the destination.

00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:09.793
Click Add index again, and click Add on AI Knowledge Base Index for Elasticsearch.

00:02:10.245 --> 00:02:15.220
Enter an Index Name and a Name, pick the Embedding deployment, which cannot

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.615
be changed later, and click Save.

00:02:21.828 --> 00:02:29.148
Open Artificial Intelligence, Data Sources, click Add Data Source, and click Add on Search Index Profile.

00:02:29.611 --> 00:02:30.766
Enter a Name.

00:02:30.766 --> 00:02:36.967
Choose the Source index, the content index, and the Destination index, the knowledge base index.

00:02:36.967 --> 00:02:40.311
The destination cannot be changed after you save.

00:02:40.798 --> 00:02:46.283
In Field Mapping, the Content field is the text to search and split into passages.

00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:49.338
The editor picks the full text of the item.

00:02:49.791 --> 00:02:54.037
The Title field is the name shown in the sources under an answer.

00:02:54.037 --> 00:02:59.298
The Key field identifies each item, so the site can update or remove its passages.

00:02:59.298 --> 00:03:01.331
You can change the defaults.

00:03:01.784 --> 00:03:02.846
Click Save.

00:03:02.846 --> 00:03:06.344
The data source starts filling its knowledge base.

00:03:10.537 --> 00:03:15.570
The data source keeps its knowledge base in step with the source index.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:20.277
To rebuild it by hand, open its Actions menu and click Sync index.

00:03:20.727 --> 00:03:23.556
The passages are created in the background.

00:03:23.556 --> 00:03:26.847
When they are ready, the assistant can search them.

00:03:31.048 --> 00:03:35.918
Open the profile, open the Knowledge tab, and choose the data source.

00:03:36.371 --> 00:03:38.721
Filter searches only some entries.

00:03:38.721 --> 00:03:43.068
It is an expression that your technical team writes, and one that is

00:03:43.068 --> 00:03:44.771
not valid is not saved.

00:03:45.227 --> 00:03:50.303
Restrict answers to retrieved data only keeps the assistant to your content.

00:03:50.303 --> 00:03:52.717
When nothing matches, it says so.

00:03:53.171 --> 00:03:58.732
Strictness is how closely a passage must match the question, from one to five.

00:03:58.732 --> 00:04:02.506
Retrieved documents is how many passages come back.

00:04:02.506 --> 00:04:03.631
Click Save.

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:10.656
Now ask a question that an article answers:

00:04:10.656 --> 00:04:13.093
how long does express shipping take?

00:04:13.548 --> 00:04:15.993
The assistant answers from the article.

00:04:15.993 --> 00:04:18.328
The statement carries a small number.

00:04:18.779 --> 00:04:23.289
Under the answer, the numbered source names the article that the answer came from.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:32.935
Profiles that leave Strictness and Retrieved documents empty use the site defaults.

00:04:32.935 --> 00:04:37.830
Open Settings, Artificial Intelligence, and find the Data Sources section.

00:04:38.301 --> 00:04:43.186
Default strictness and Default top documents are the values that every data source

00:04:43.186 --> 00:04:45.961
uses when a profile does not choose its own.

00:04:50.161 --> 00:04:51.320
Help articles:

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:55.491
the assistant answers from the articles that your editors publish.

00:04:56.241 --> 00:04:57.108
Products:

00:04:57.108 --> 00:05:00.631
it knows the catalog, and the answer names the product.

00:05:01.381 --> 00:05:02.939
News and policies:

00:05:02.939 --> 00:05:05.991
change a page, and the knowledge follows.

00:05:06.741 --> 00:05:08.110
Several sources:

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:12.091
more than one data source can feed a knowledge base index.

00:05:14.091 --> 00:05:18.283
Index your content, link it to a knowledge base with a data source,

00:05:18.283 --> 00:05:20.178
and choose it on a profile.

00:05:20.178 --> 00:05:23.738
The assistant then answers from your site, with sources.

00:05:23.738 --> 00:05:25.231
Thanks for watching.

